# Enforce consistent line endings — LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# The Git for Windows installer sets core.autocrlf=true in the system config, so without
# this file a Windows clone gets CRLF working files. That would break byte-comparison of
# the vendored VS Code files against upstream, which ships LF:
#
#   src/renderer/css/markdown.css
#   src/renderer/css/highlight.css
#   src/renderer/slugify.ts
#
# Those three are kept verbatim so they can be re-diffed against the vscode repo — see
# licenses/NOTICE.md. Local deviations belong in a separate overrides file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Source — LF
*.ts text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.rs text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.svg text eol=lf

# Config, lockfiles and docs — LF
*.json text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.lock text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf

# Binary — no conversion, no text diffing
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
